Title: LOW TIDE
Author: Vincent Marchetti
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. HARBOR - ESTABLISHING - NIGHT

Working docks. Fog rolls in. Trawlers creak at moorings.

INT. FISHING TRAWLER - WHEELHOUSE - NIGHT

CAPTAIN EDDIE MORAN steers. CALLAHAN spots a dark contact on radar.
CALLAHAN
Coast Guard doesn't run dark.

EXT. TRAWLER DECK - NIGHT

Covert exchange — fish out, shrink-wrapped cargo in.

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - NIGHT

DETECTIVE SARAH PELL maps three identical runs. DUNN skeptical.
PELL
Same fog bank. Same blind spot. Moran's boat every time.

INT. PELL'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Case files spread on the table. Photos of Eddie with his daughter at a pier picnic.
PELL
He's not a kingpin. He's a paycheck.

INT. DOCKSIDE BAR - NIGHT

Pell confronts Eddie. He stays calm, tired.
EDDIE
You come with proof or sympathy.

EXT. HOSPITAL - DAY

Pell learns Eddie's daughter starts chemo next week — bills pinned to a fridge photo in the file.
DUNN
That doesn't make the run legal.

INT. WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Surveillance: Eddie meets a buyer in a yellow slicker — not his usual contact.
PELL
Someone new is using his route.

INT. TRAWLER HOLD - NIGHT

Pell and a tac team board — empty hold, trapdoor open to the water.
EDDIE
I didn't run tonight. They used my name.

EXT. HARBOR - PREDAWN

Eddie in cuffs on the pier. Pell watches the real smuggler boat vanish into fog. She has a bigger fish — and a smaller man to cut loose.
PELL
Tell me who owns the yellow slicker. Then we talk about your daughter.

FADE OUT.


THE END
